From: Matt
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-msm8994: give the PCIe aux RCGs a parent map

Like usb3_phy_aux_clk_src (patch 0024): the PCIe aux clock sources use P_XO
in their frequency table but have no parent_map, so nobody can set their
rate (clk_set_rate() dereferences NULL) and the aux clock stays as the
bootloader left it, which does not set PCIe up. CAF runs it at 1.01 MHz
(pci-msm.c msm_pcie_clk_info). XO is the first entry of gcc_xo_gpll0_map.
---
diff -ruN a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8994.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8994.c
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8994.c	2026-10-28 01:10:08.206484093 +0100
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8994.c	2026-10-28 01:10:08.218468372 +0100
@@ -862,6 +862,8 @@
 	.cmd_rcgr = 0x1b00,
 	.mnd_width = 8,
 	.hid_width = 5,
+	/* without a map, clk_set_rate() dereferences NULL */
+	.parent_map = gcc_xo_gpll0_map,
 	.freq_tbl = ftbl_pcie_0_aux_clk_src,
 	.clkr.hw.init = &(struct clk_init_data){
 		.name = "pcie_0_aux_clk_src",
@@ -921,6 +923,8 @@
 	.cmd_rcgr = 0x1b80,
 	.mnd_width = 8,
 	.hid_width = 5,
+	/* without a map, clk_set_rate() dereferences NULL */
+	.parent_map = gcc_xo_gpll0_map,
 	.freq_tbl = ftbl_pcie_1_aux_clk_src,
 	.clkr.hw.init = &(struct clk_init_data){
 		.name = "pcie_1_aux_clk_src",
